                                                "sense_id": "4e840e56-14a6-39d2-87e8-d417ef17fe80",
                                                "text": "Here it was that, guarded by double doors, Sir Francis smoked cigars, and read Bell’s Life in London, and went to sleep after dinner, when he was not smoking over the billiard-table at his clubs, or punting at the gambling-houses in Saint James’s."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1453c1e5-9bb8-3f08-b6ca-d62de4bc3051",
                                        "entry_id": "b673f3cf-9de2-3f27-8e22-cbcea5dc61a8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To stake against the bank, to back a horse, to gamble or take a chance more generally"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "Ireland",
                                            "New-Zealand",
                                            "UK"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "daa6a01a-6b56-4a90-a05e-b80ba46b8711",
                                                "sense_id": "1453c1e5-9bb8-3f08-b6ca-d62de4bc3051",
                                                "text": "She heard […] of his punting at gaming tables."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf8987e2-7326-45ea-af71-73d2618b8ab7",
                                                "sense_id": "1453c1e5-9bb8-3f08-b6ca-d62de4bc3051",
                                                "text": "Whether you want to gamble on a horse race, bet on which player will score first in a game of football, have a punt on a particular tennis player winning a grand slam event, you are buying a chance, a chance which is measured in terms of probability, ‘the odds’."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93f6b62e-e4e7-4698-ba6c-cf99d473e01e",
                                                "sense_id": "1453c1e5-9bb8-3f08-b6ca-d62de4bc3051",
                                                "text": "Eriksson's men still worth a punt"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bae76b0d-5856-4b28-93ec-3d825aa0a4db",
                                                "sense_id": "1453c1e5-9bb8-3f08-b6ca-d62de4bc3051",
                                                "text": "Australians have a reputation for being keen to bet on two flies climbing up a wall and today young ones often take a casual classroom punt"
                                            }
                                        ]
